 "type": "manga",
 "attributes": {
  "title": {
   "en": "Gokuraku Ni Wa Mada Hayai"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja": "極楽にはまだ早い"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "A tale of Yukinari, a beheading executioner known as a ‘manslayer,’ and the people around him in the town of Yaokyacho. In the Edo period (1603-1868), where the story takes place, most people who committed crimes were executed. One day, Saichiro, the son of a town doctor, is present when Yukinari slays a criminal. Later, Saichiro sees Yukinari ignoring his family members who are begging for the life of a criminal. He turns to Yukinari, who looks as if he doesn't care about people, and asks him if he doesn't even listen to him. Saichiro is dissatisfied with the answer, but then something happens. The story of a man who lives and dies by killing people unfolds.",
   "ja": "「極楽にはまだ早い」は、“人斬り”と呼ばれた斬首の執行人・雪成と、彼を取り巻く人々の八百八町人情譚。物語の舞台となる江戸時代では、罪を犯した者のほとんどが処刑となっていた。町医者の息子・佐一郎は、ある日雪成が罪人を斬るところに居合わせる。その後、罪人の命乞いをする家族を無視する雪成を目にした佐一郎。人を人と思っていないような表情の雪成に向かい、話も聞いてやらないのかと問いかけると「私は ただ 刑を執行するだけだ」と雪成は言い放つ。その答えに不満を持つ佐一郎だったが、ある出来事が起こり……。人を斬り、生きる男の物語が展開される。"
  },
